	"comments": [
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A lone `>` that ends a line is where tsc settles a type-argument list: its recovering",
			"start": 20,
			"end": 108
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " parse runs from an earlier `<` to the first token it cannot take, and a line break past a",
			"start": 110,
			"end": 202
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " `>` there commits the region. So the one break this `>` takes is the one AHEAD of it.",
			"start": 204,
			"end": 292
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " The shelled operand's line is exactly 100, and stays flat.",
			"start": 295,
			"end": 356
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " One character longer: 101, so the operand breaks — ahead of its `>`, never after it.",
			"start": 476,
			"end": 563
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " No shell at all: a comma is a type-argument separator, so a sibling `>` closes the region",
			"start": 687,
			"end": 779
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " an earlier argument's `<` opened. Exactly 100 stays flat.",
			"start": 781,
			"end": 841
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " 101 breaks ahead of the `>`.",
			"start": 961,
			"end": 992
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " The pair around a kept-shell chain answers the OUTER `>` alone, so that one still ends its",
			"start": 1116,
			"end": 1209
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " line; the inner one is the first the region reaches, and leads its own.",
			"start": 1211,
			"end": 1285
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " An arrow body and an array head reach the same `>` through a function type and a tuple.",
			"start": 1426,
			"end": 1516
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A `<<` opens the region as a `<` does: tsc re-scans it to one where it looks for type",
			"start": 1792,
			"end": 1880
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " arguments.",
			"start": 1882,
			"end": 1895
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A conditional's branch, an index and an object member reach the `>` through an optional",
			"start": 2027,
			"end": 2117
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " parameter, an indexed access type and a type literal.",
			"start": 2119,
			"end": 2175
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " A block body inside the region is still inside it: the arrow's braces read as a type",
			"start": 2601,
			"end": 2688
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " literal, and `return (` as a method signature.",
			"start": 2690,
			"end": 2739
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " Where the region has ended, the `>` ends its line as any operator does: a statement's",
			"start": 2905,
			"end": 2993
		},
		{
			"type": "Line",
			"value": " head says nothing about its body, and the `)` of the call the `<` was written in closes it.",
			"start": 2995,
			"end": 3089
		}
	],
